From 705660a268f6eb875a00b929998480368842b2fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojavemesa-lgtm <252102886+mojavemesa-lgtm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:32:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] power: supply: qcom_smbx: Leave the Type-C role
 register to the port driver

The SMB2 init sequence programs TYPE_C_INTRPT_ENB_SOFTWARE_CTRL (power
role command and VCONN enable) with a "FIXME: This will be handled by
the type-c driver" note. The new qcom,pmi8998-typec port driver now
handles it and writes the same register for role switching, so the
charger's init write would reset the role that the port driver chose
whenever the charger probes.

Detect an available qcom,pmi8998-typec sibling node at probe and skip
that one register in the init sequence.

Tested on a OnePlus 6T (fajita) together with the Type-C port driver:
automatic sink/source switching works and the charger no longer touches
the register.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 9386adfb7..01f98287c 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -248,6 +248,9 @@ struct smb_chip {
 	struct iio_channel *usb_in_v_chan;
 
 	struct power_supply *chg_psy;
+
+	/* An enabled Type-C port driver owns the CC role/VCONN register */
+	bool typec_owned;
 };
 
 struct smb_match_data {
@@ -934,6 +937,9 @@ static int smb_init_hw(struct smb_chip *chip, const struct smb_init_register *in
 	int rc, i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
+		if (chip->typec_owned &&
+		    init_seq[i].addr == TYPE_C_INTRPT_ENB_SOFTWARE_CTRL)
+			continue;
 		dev_dbg(chip->dev, "%d: Writing 0x%02x to 0x%02x\n", i,
 			init_seq[i].val, init_seq[i].addr);
 		rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
@@ -1013,6 +1019,18 @@ static int smb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	dev_info(chip->dev, "Generation %s\n", chip->gen == SMB2 ? "SMB2" : "SMB5");
 
+	if (chip->gen == SMB2) {
+		struct device_node *np;
+
+		for_each_available_child_of_node(pdev->dev.parent->of_node, np) {
+			if (of_device_is_compatible(np, "qcom,pmi8998-typec")) {
+				chip->typec_owned = true;
+				of_node_put(np);
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	rc = smb_init_hw(chip, match_data->init_seq, match_data->init_seq_len);
 	if (rc < 0)
 		return rc;
